From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slothfulchat <patches@slothfulchat.invalid>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 22:38:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 79/82] web-app: copy text from a multi-message selection
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Selecting a second message collapsed the context menu to Forward and
Delete. "Copy Text" is the obvious third entry there, so add it — plus
Ctrl/Cmd + C on a focused selection — putting the selected message bodies
on the clipboard, one per line.

Messages without text (stickers, bare images, files, webxdc) drop out
rather than becoming `[photo.jpg]` placeholder lines — that is transcript
formatting, and Export Chat already writes real transcripts. A caption is
text and gets copied; a not-yet-downloaded message contributes what is on
screen, i.e. its caption without the appended "[Label – size]" tag, same
as the single-message action. If nothing in the selection has text the
write is failed instead of blanking the clipboard; that can only be known
after the fetch, so the menu entry itself is always shown.

The keyboard path sits with the other per-message shortcuts in
`onKeyDown` (Ctrl + E/R/S, Delete) and shares `copyMessagesText()` with
the menu. It only fires when the DOM selection is empty: a text selection
means the user wants the browser's own copy, the same preference
`buildContextMenu` encodes by offering "Copy Selection" over "Copy Text".

The selection can span messages the list never loaded — a Shift + click
range covers the whole chat, not just the rendered window — so the text
comes from a `getMessages` round-trip. Browsers only honour a clipboard
write inside the user gesture that triggered it, and awaiting that RPC
first loses transient activation on WebKit, which then rejects the write.
`writeClipboardText()` therefore also accepts a `Promise<string>`, and the
browser targets hand it straight to `ClipboardItem` instead of awaiting;
the Electron and Tauri targets just await it as before.

Ordering is fixed for Forward and Delete along the way: `selectedItems`
is a `Set` in click order, so Ctrl + clicking bottom-up used to forward
and delete in reverse. The message list's own chronological ids are now
exposed on `MessageMultiselectContext`, and both the menu and the
keyboard handler filter those.
